<!--META-DATA
{
	tags: vector, logical, min,
}
-->

<statement>
<p>
	This function determines if an undirected graph is Eulerian. An Eulerian graph is a connected graph that can traverse every edge exactly once and return to the starting point.
</p>

<tabular valign="top" top="minor">
	<col width="12%"/>
	<col width="88%"/>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell>Inputs:</cell>
		<cell>
			<p><pf>G</pf> (struct) number — : A structure representing the graph containing, at minimum, the following fields:</p>
			<p><pf>G.degrees</pf> (n x 1) double vector — : A column vector where each element represents the degree of a corresponding vertex in the graph.</p>
			<p><pf>G.connected</pf> (1 x 1, logical) logical — : <pf>true</pf> if the graph is connected. <pf>false</pf>, otherwise</p>
		</cell>
	</row>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell>Outputs:</cell>
		<cell>
			<p><pf>result</pf> (logical) logical — : Returns true if the graph is Eulerian (all vertices have even degree), false otherwise.</p>
		</cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell>Details:</cell>
		<cell><p>To code this, use the theorem: "A connected graph is Eulerian if every vertex has an even degree."</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>Command Window Expected Output G.connected = true; G.degrees = [2; 2; 2; 2]; result = HW5P8_is_eulerian(G); result = logical 1 G.connected = true; G.degrees = [1; 2; 3; 2]; result = HW5P8_is_eulerian(G); result = logical 0 G.connected = false; G.degrees = [1; 2; 3; 2]; result = HW5P8_is_eulerian(G); result = logical 0 G.connected = true; G.degrees = [0]; result = HW5P8_is_eulerian(G); result = logical 1</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>Expected Output</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>result = logical 1</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>result = logical 0</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>result = logical 0</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>result = logical 1</p></cell>
	</row>
</tabular>

</statement>
